CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-011: Screwdriver Antenna — 6m Band
CM  Whip retracted to 1.40m (VHF tip section only), NO loading coil
CM  Frequency: 50.000–54.000 MHz (9 points, 0.500 MHz step)
CM
CM  Configuration: screwdriver coil fully retracted / bypassed.
CM  Only the upper VHF tip section (1.40m) is in use.
CM  1.40m = 0.233 lambda at 50 MHz (slightly short of QW = 1.50m)
CM  No loading coil; slight capacitive reactance remains.
CM  For best SWR, tip may need to be 1.48-1.52m depending on
CM  mount capacitance and vehicle body coupling.
CM
CM  Whip: 1.40m, avg radius 0.006m, 10 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 1.40m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM  No LD card (no loading coil on 6m)
CM
CM  Tuning note: 6m is "the magic band." Pattern on this model
CM  shows typical monopole behavior — omnidirectional in azimuth,
CM  with peak radiation angle near 20-25 deg elevation at 50 MHz.
CM  Ground-wave propagation is significant on 6m; radial system
CM  quality affects low-angle gain more than on HF bands.
CM  Sporadic-E, TEP, and F2 openings all benefit from low-angle.
CM ============================================================
CE
GW 1  10  0 0 0       0 0 1.40    0.006
GW 2   4  0 0 0.005   1.40 0 0.005  0.006
GW 3   4  0 0 0.005  -1.40 0 0.005  0.006
GW 4   4  0 0 0.005   0 1.40 0.005  0.006
GW 5   4  0 0 0.005   0 -1.40 0.005 0.006
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
EX 0  1  1  0  1  0
FR 0  9  0  0  50.000  0.500
RP 0  37  73  1000  0  0  5  5
EN
